In the evening, I sit on my sofa with my computer.
I call my family in Mexico.
The screen shows my parents, my sister Sofía, and my brother Diego.
Our dog, Lola, is there too.
"Happy birthday!" they all shout.
Sofía asks.
"Have you received our package?"
"Yes, it arrived in the mail yesterday," I answer.
"Have you opened it?" she asks excitedly.
I smile and take a colorful scarf from the table.
"I opened it when I came home," I say and hold the scarf up.
"I really love the colors."
I put the scarf around my neck.
"It suits you well," my mother says.
"Have you had a good day today?" my father asks.
"Yes, my colleagues bought a cake for me earlier," I explain.
Diego lifts Lola up to the camera.
"Lola has also eaten a little cake," he laughs.
I laugh loudly at the little dog.
It is my first birthday away from home, but they feel very close.
